  "_commit": {
    "id": "b40b4e648d88d06351951a3ebf57f010ad4f6a89",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "Fall back gracefully when nanoarrow is unavailable for Arrow-export fetch\n\nwriteDuckDBTableParquet()'s schema-sampling step unconditionally fetches\nvia DuckDB's Arrow export (dbSendQueryArrow()/dbFetchArrow()), which\nrequires the nanoarrow package. duckdb itself only lists nanoarrow under\nSuggests, so it is not guaranteed to be installed wherever duckdb is --\nthis broke every BiocDuckDB test calling writeParquet() on Bioconductor's\nnebbiolo2 builder, which lacks it.\n\nAdd nanoarrow to Suggests and guard the fetch with\nrequireNamespace(\"nanoarrow\", quietly = TRUE), falling back to the\npre-optimization full-file reread when it is absent, so its absence is\nnever a hard error.\n",
    "time": 1794091694
  },
